    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d175-a3">

                <pb facs="0339" n="243" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg243"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 159.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr. Dutton.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Pelting, China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-03-11"><hi rendition="#italic">March 11,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I can not permit you to leave this legation
                    with your marine guard without expressing my complete satisfaction with the
                    service <pb facs="0340" n="244" xml:id="pg244"/> rendered and most heartily
                    commending both you and your men for the incomparable manner in which it has
                    been performed.</p>
                <p>The conduct of the men has uniformly been above criticism, and their duties at
                    all times admirably performed.</p>
                <p>This all evidences remarkable discipline and most constant, careful, and
                    intelligent official supervision.</p>
                <p>For all of which I desire to express my sincere appreciation, and to offer to
                    you, personally, my grateful acknowledgments.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
